{"name":"Winter Coat","hex":"#45494c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winter coat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A warm coat, often an overcoat, fit to be worn in winter","An animal's seasonal appearance in winter, notably thicker and/or otherwise camouflaged plumage or fur after (often autumnal) moulting"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winter_coat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coat","blocks":[{"text":"A coat is an outer garment for the upper body, worn by any gender for warmth or fashion. Coats typically have long sleeves and are open down the front, and closing by means of buttons, zippers, hook-and-loop fasteners, toggles, a belt, or a combination of some of these. Other possible features include collars, shoulder straps, and hoods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg/330px-FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coat","wikidata":"Q152574"},{"title":"Animal coat","blocks":[{"text":"Coat is the nature and quality of a mammal's fur. In the animal fancy, coat is an attribute that reflects the quality of a specimen's breeding as well as the level of the animal's care, conditioning, and management. Coat is an integral aspect of the judging at competitions, such as a conformation dog show, a cat show, a horse show, or a rabbit show."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Mustela_winter.jpg/330px-Mustela_winter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_coat","wikidata":"Q1817674"},{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt 